cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software release and the accompanying methodological paper."
title: "Unified Ornstein–Uhlenbeck–Lévy–Branching Framework"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-05"

authors:
  - family-names: "Kim"
    given-names: "Seung-Hwan"

abstract: >-
  The Unified Ornstein–Uhlenbeck–Lévy–Branching (OULB) Framework is a
  probabilistic and computational framework for modeling biological evolution
  through continuous Ornstein–Uhlenbeck dynamics, abrupt Lévy-like transitions,
  lineage branching, heterogeneous observation models, and Bayesian inference.
  The repository includes a reproducible pediatric leukemia reference
  application, simulation benchmarks, regression tests, and scripts for
  generating all manuscript figures.

keywords:
  - computational biology
  - cancer evolution
  - pediatric leukemia
  - Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process
  - Levy process
  - branching process
  - Bayesian inference
  - stochastic processes
  - single-cell transcriptomics
  - reproducible research

